- text[value="Trash"]
::::

Items stay 30 days, then delete forever; restoring puts them back where they were.

::::row[icon=doc href=#]
Q3 pricing scratchpad
Doc · deleted Aug 04 · 29 days left
action: Restore | restoreTrashItem
action: Delete forever | deleteTrashItemForever
::::

::::row[icon=file href=#]
hero-draft-2.png
File · deleted Aug 02 · 27 days left
action: Restore | restoreTrashItem
action: Delete forever | deleteTrashItemForever
::::

:::

::

Every row carries the trailing action pair: Restore returns the item to where it lived (and removes it from this list); Delete forever is the danger action, ALWAYS last in the pair, and asks nothing further — the 30-day window was the grace period. Days-left counts down in the row meta. The Settings-root Trash row mirrors the live count ("2 items · auto-deletes after 30 days"). When the list is empty the pane shows the muted note "Trash is empty." The title row is circled back + title only — no actions to convert (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11); Restore and Delete forever keep their labels as meaning-carrying row actions. At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the shell contract applies unchanged: sidebar behind the generated tab-bar + FAB, the 880px column full-width with edge padding, and the rows with their trailing action pair flow full-width and stay visible at touch widths.
